==English==
{{swp}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|en|sound|track}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsaʊndˌtɹæk/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-soundtrack.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[narrow]] [[strip]] running down a [[movie]] [[film]] that carries the [[recorded]] [[sound]] in [[synchronization]] with the [[picture]]s.
# The sound (especially the [[music]]) component of a movie, video game, etc.
# A [[recording]] or [[compilation]] of recordings of such music for [[sale]].
# A [[background]] [[sound]] that is part of a larger [[event]].
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=2014-08-16|author=Daniel Taylor|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/aug/16/manchester-united-swansea-city-premier-league-match-report|title=Swansea upstage Manchester United in Louis van Gaal’s Premier League bow|passage=
There was a startling lack of creativity and if Van Gaal had listened closely he would have made out the mocking chants from the away end, as the visiting fans embarked on the repertoire of songs that formed the '''soundtrack''' to David Moyes’s time in the job.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250831001018/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/aug/16/manchester-united-swansea-city-premier-league-match-report}}
# [[popular music|Popular music]] associated with a particular historical [[era]] or time of one's life, especially [[nostalgically]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''soundtrack''' of our relationship}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-04-05|author=Victor Brooks|title=Last Season of Innocence: The Teen Experience in the 1960s|publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing PLC|isbn=9781442209183|page=194
|text=CDs, iPods, and other forms of digital downloading, large numbers of specialty music channels or digitalized television services, satellite radio, and related media, all mean that anyone interested in the '''soundtrack''' of the sixties can access any song at any time in almost any place — a dream unbelievable to a sixties teen carrying his or her transistor radio.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2026-03-07|author=Daphne A. Brooks|title=Blackstar Rising and the Purple Reign: The Sonic Afterlives of David Bowie and Prince|publisher=Duke University Press|isbn=9781478062059
|text=But in my young mind, nothing was haphazard, and certain songs that came over the car radio became fundamental parts of the resonating '''soundtrack''' of my youth.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.jewishnews.co.uk/opinion-tom-lehrer-the-musical-comedy-soundtrack-of-my-childhood/|date=August 21, 2025|author=Darren Richman|title=OPINION: Tom Lehrer – the musical comedy '''soundtrack''' of my childhood|work=Jewish News|passage={{quote-gloss|See title}}|archiveurl= https://web.archive.org/web/20250829180629/https://www.jewishnews.co.uk/opinion-tom-lehrer-the-musical-comedy-soundtrack-of-my-childhood/}}

